{"id":102,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"These Pokémon get nervous when they’re not in a group of six. The minute even one member of the group goes missing, Exeggcute become cowardly."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Though it may look like it’s just a bunch of eggs, it’s a proper Pokémon. Exeggcute communicates with others of its kind via telepathy, apparently."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"The heads attract each other and spin around. There must be six heads for it to maintain balance."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Although they are the same size as other Exeggcute, the ones produced in Alola are quite heavy. Their shells are packed full."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Six of them form a single Pokémon. Should one of the six be lost, the next morning there will once more be six."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Six of them together form a full-fledged Pokémon. It’s often hunted by Crabrawler, but uses psychokinesis to drive it off."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Its six eggs use telepathy to communicate among themselves. It is believed to carry plant genes and the genes of other species."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"This Pokémon consists of six eggs that form a closely knit cluster. The six eggs attract each other and spin around. When cracks increasingly appear on the eggs, Exeggcute is close to evolution."},{"games":["Y","FireRed"],"text":"Even though it appears to be eggs of some sort, it was discovered to be a life-form more like plant seeds."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Its six eggs converse using telepathy. They can quickly gather if they become separated."},{"games":["SoulSilver"],"text":"Using telepathy only they can employ, they always form a cluster of six EXEGGCUTE."},{"games":["HeartGold"],"text":"Their shells are very durable. Even if they crack, they can survive without spilling their contents."},{"games":["LeafGreen"],"text":"It is often mistaken for eggs. When disturbed, they quickly gather and attack in swarms."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It consists of six eggs that care for each other. The eggs attract each other and spin around. When cracks increasingly appear, it is close to evolution."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Chlorophyll","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in harsh sunlight."},{"name":"Harvest","hidden":true,"description":"May create another Berry after one is used."}],"eggGroups":["Grass"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"forest","color":"Pink","shape":"Heads","evolution":{"id":102,"name":"Exeggcute","condition":null,"children":[{"id":103,"name":"Exeggutor","condition":"Use Leaf Stone or Use Leaf Stone, in Alola","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,71],[1,95],[5,115],[10,73],[15,72],[20,93],[25,235],[30,331],[35,202],[40,326],[45,253],[50,388],[55,76]],"machine":[331,174,203,412,263,202,447,803,580,270,286,437,113,182,60,244,94,917,473,115,156,402,285,214,188,76,500,164,241,14,851,168,271,253,428],"egg":[246,335,174,275,236,77,79,78],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv8-192","name":"Exeggcute","set":"Surging Sparks","date":"2024-11-08","rarity":"Illustration Rare","number":"192","artist":null,"img":"sv8/192"},{"id":"me55-1","name":"Exeggcute","set":"30th Celebration","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Common","number":"1","artist":"Nelnal","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-1/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55-1/large"},{"id":"me2pt5-77","name":"Team Rocket's Exeggcute","set":"Ascended Heroes","date":"2026-01-30","rarity":"Common","number":"77","artist":"Gapao","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-77/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-77/large"},{"id":"me1-4","name":"Exeggcute","set":"Mega Evolution","date":"2025-09-26","rarity":"Common","number":"4","artist":null,"img":"me1/4"},{"id":"sv8pt5-1","name":"Ex